T*
(We have surveyed hundreds of aircraft maintenance and GS technicians and) Tj
T*
(engineers and managers, tech-ops procurement personnel and EOM production) Tj
T*
(engineers to estimate the incidence of Maintenance and Production related) Tj
T*
(Covered Pitot Events \(COPES\). Our results indicate that an average capacity MRO) Tj
T*
(station performing medium and heavy maintenance experiences three COPES) Tj
T*
(yearly causing damaged pitot probes from covers being left in place on heated) Tj
T*
(pitot tubes while testing systems. The actual number is unknown and is likely) Tj
T*
(higher given hesitancy to report. Assuming three probes damaged per incident,) Tj
T*
(we developed the following engineering-economic model based on typical) Tj
T*
(commercial MRO and OEM operations. Because OEMs, Airlines and MROs do not) Tj
T*
(publish these events, the assumptions are necessarily estimates, but they are) Tj
T*
(consistent with industry replacement costs and operational impacts.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
